\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The road to Liese Academy hasn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t changed, not in all these years.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 First, the Deep Woods. A name that sounds far more mysterious than it really is. In truth, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s just miles of trees packed too close together, a canopy so thick the morning light can barely slip through. Riding under it always feels like diving into a tunnel of shadows\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 cold air in my lungs, damp earth under my tires, branches whispering secrets I\u8217\'92d rather not hear. The silence there presses close, broken only by the crunch of gravel beneath my wheels.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 I almost pedaled straight into them before I saw them: a knot of men gathered off the trail, half-hidden by the trees. Hunters, by the look of them. A patchwork of chain, leather, and dented steel. Half of them carried matchlock rifles so rusted I doubted they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d survive a spark, while the rest swung axes and swords like they\u8217\'92d been born with them.}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 I skidded my bike to a stop, gravel crunching too loud in the hush. Every head turned.}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Who are you?\u8221\'94 I ask, because subtlety is my strong suit.}
\par\plain {A man with a goatee and a pike steps forward, blood on his knuckles and a grin that says he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s used to being in charge. \u8220\'93Fredrick,\u8221\'94 he says. He jerks his chin toward the others. \u8220\'93This is Rika the Huntress, Clover the Healer, Owen and Rowan\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 sharpshooters. We\u8217\'92re Hunters from King\u8217\'92s Grave. We collect bounties for slain monsters.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Slain monsters?\u8221\'94 I repeat, because apparently I\u8217\'92ve been living under a rock that also happens to be on a cliff.}
\par\plain {Rika, who\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s midway through skinning the thing, looks up and snorts. \u8220\'93Aye. The mayor\u8217\'92s been bleedin\u8217\'92 about more beasts turnin\u8217\'92 up. Paladins won\u8217\'92t come, so they put up coin\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and here we are.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Hey, didn\u8217\'92t one of the council folk said they called in an expert from Edenfield,\u8221\'94 Rowan says, wiping his hands on a bit of cloth. \u8220\'93Supposedly something big\u8217\'92s been movin\u8217\'92 this way.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Owen scoffs without taking his eyes off the carcass. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93What use\u8217\'92s a posh twat from Edenfield for? We\u8217\'92re dealin with monsters, not books!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Fredrick turns his attention back to me. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re a local, then? Where d\u8217\'92you live?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s um\u8230\'85\u8221\'94 I stuttered}
\par\plain {Owen perks up. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Don\u8217\'92t worry\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 ain\u8217\'92t like we\u8217\'92re gonna sack your homes. We\u8217\'92ll be rich after this!\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Shut up, Owen,\u8221\'94 Rika snaps, not even looking away from her knife. \u8220\'93You\u8217\'92re scarin\u8217\'92 the boy.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93Go on,\u8221\'94 Fredrick said, \u8220\'93It\u8217\'92s alright.\u8221\'94}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f1\fs24\b0\i0 \loch\af1\hich\af1\dbch\af1\uc1\u8220\'93Past the forest,\u8221\'94 I say. \u8220\'93Near the cliffs\hich\f1 \emdash \loch\f1 old lighthouse.\u8221\'94}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {Clover, who\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s been gently probing the beast\u8217\'92s wounds like she\u8217\'92s checking a patient\u8217\'92s pulse, frowns. \u8220\'93There\u8217\'92s no guards out near the lighthouse, is there? You\u8217\'92ll be all right?\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93We\u8217\'92re fine.\u8221\'94 I shrug, trying for breezy and landing somewhere between defensive and proud. \u8220\'93My mother put a ring around the place. Keeps the arcane nasties out\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 so far.\u8221\'94}
\par\plain {Everything goes quiet. The forest listens.}
\par\plain {Fredrick studies me, then nods slowly, like he\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s put two and two together and gotten a number that makes him uneasy. \u8220\'93Ah. So you\u8217\'92re one of them.\u8221\'94 He says it like it\u8217\'92s a label, not an insult\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 then, as if that settles something, \u8220\'93Carry on, then. Best be careful.\u8221\'94}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The Hunters drifted back into their huddle, already talking of tracks and traps and things I didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t want to picture. I pushed off again, wheels cracking twigs as I left them behind\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 feeling the shadows a little heavier than before.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 -o-}
\par\pard\plain \ltrch\loch 
\par\plain {My mind was still back in the Deep Woods, replaying every rough voice and rusted blade, when I realized I\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d pedaled straight into Weshaven. The place announces itself with the smell first\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 salt air tangled with fish guts, tar, and bread pulled fresh from ovens. Then the sights: sails from foreign ships crowding the harbor, merchants shouting over each other in accents I couldn\u8217\'92t place, coins flashing from one palm to another. }
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {The town greets you all at once\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 salt air from the harbor, smoke from chimneys, and the sharp smell of fish that somehow manages to sneak into everything. Ships with foreign flags bob along the docks, unloading crates stamped in languages I can\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t read, while merchants haggle in at least three accents I can. The cobblestone streets twist through stalls crammed with spices, trinkets, and enough bread to make you question whether wheat is their true religion. Kids race between carts, chased by shopkeepers who swear like poets.}
\par\plain {And the people\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 Weshaven is full of them. Dockhands, traders, sailors, and travelers in cloaks that don\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t belong to this climate. Everyone moving like they\u8217\'92ve got somewhere important to be, even if it\u8217\'92s just the next alehouse.}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {And then there were the Hunters. Apparently half the realm got the memo I missed. They came in every flavor: some with armor polished enough to blind, some in mismatched junk held together with luck, and a few in matching heraldry like they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d wandered off the pages of a knightly ballad. Most looked like they\u8217\'92d just thrown on whatever wouldn\u8217\'92t fall off mid-battle. Nearly all of them were streaming toward the town hall, no doubt to line up for bounties. Which meant my earlier encounter hadn\u8217\'92t been a fluke\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 something nasty was definitely nesting nearby, and everyone with a sharp stick wanted in.}
\par\pard\plain \sa180\sb180\ltrch\loch {I kept pedaling, wheels clattering over uneven stones, doing my best to look like just out on an errand\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 and not like someone who\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d just biked out of a forest full of monsters and mercenaries.}
\par\plain {But the real trial started at the bottom of Easmund Hill. Out here, it was mostly farmland\hich\f0 \emdash \loch\f0 rows of plants stretching on forever. The slope didn\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92t look steep from a distance, but my thigh disagreed. Turns out I\u8217\'92m not nearly as nimble or strong as my younger self. Back then I could fly up this road, calves like iron, lungs like bellows. Now every push of the pedals felt like a personal betrayal from my own body.}
\par\plain {From down here, I could already see the Academy. The biggest thing on the hill, stone walls rising like they\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92d grown straight out of the earth, nestled right between two endless fields of sugarcane. The towers caught the light in a way that made the place look less like a school and more like a monument someone forgot to label. And me, huffing and puffing at its doorstep, wondering whether I\u8217\'92d make it up there alive enough to appreciate the architecture.}}